  "solution": {
    "text": "The total number of optically active compounds formed is four. The product has two chiral $\\mathrm{C}$ atoms. Thus, it has $2^n=2^2=4$ stereoisomers.\n<img src=\"assets\\st0337_2e4430d1aa0d.png\"><br><img src=\"assets\\st0337_29485eba5ed1.png\"><br>"
  }
